    "authors_year": "Luis Angel García-Escudero, Alfonso Gordaliza & Carlos Matrán, 2003",
    "research_question": "How can trimmed k-means and related variance functionals be used as exploratory graphical tools to distinguish between the bulk of data (proper clusters) and outlying observations, determine the number of groups ($k$), and characterize cluster sizes?",
    "methods": [
      "Trimmed k-means methodology using impartial trimming (minimizing within-groups variance over subsets of size $n(1-\\alpha)$).",
      "Exploratory graphical tools based on trimmed $k$-variance functionals (plotting empirical trimmed $k$-variance against trimming size $\\alpha$) and their numerical second derivatives.",
      "An algorithm for computing trimmed $k$-means combining random seed initializations, a modified \"K-mean-step\" (adapted from the FAST-MCD algorithm), and nonrandom sequential initializations.",
      "Generalization to mixtures of elliptical distributions by replacing spherical distance measures with scatter estimation matrices minimizing $\\sum_{i=1}^k n_i \\log(\\det(W_i/n_i))$."
    ],
    "main_findings": [
